---
import Component from "../../components/PageNarrowBody.astro";
import "../../styles/tokens.css";

// The narrow block a chapter page and a community page both end with: back
// link, leads, markdown body, then the entry's own links.
//
// It was written twice — once in each page shell — when communities got their
// own page type, differing only in the leads heading and the back-link wording.
// That is the shape that drifts: a spacing or accessibility fix applied to one
// copy silently leaves the other behind. Capturing it once, here, is what makes
// the two pages provably share it.
//
// The fixture is the community configuration (a named lead under a "Community
// Lead" heading) because it exercises every slot at once — a chapter renders
// the same block with a different heading.
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Isolated: PageNarrowBody</title>
  </head>
  <body style="margin: 0; min-height: 100vh; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;">
    <div id="codeyam-capture" style="width: 100%;">
      <Component
        backHref="/#community"
        backLabel="← All communities"
        leads={[{ name: 'James Nicholson', role: 'Community Lead (pilot)' }]}
        leadsHeading="Community Lead"
        links={[
          { label: 'Join the WhatsApp', url: 'https://forms.gle/GqgaCDDWhWAgpJC68' },
          { label: 'Past call notes', url: '/blog/welcome' },
        ]}
        hasBody={true}
      >
        <p>
          A cross-chapter community for Harvard alumni working in AI — researchers,
          founders, product leaders, and the people deploying it inside larger companies.
        </p>
      </Component>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
